---
title: FieldErrors
description: Renders the validation-error container for a field — a live region whose ID is added to the control's aria-describedby while errors exist.
---

<script>
	import LiveFieldDemo from "$lib/demos/live-field-demo.svelte";
</script>

`FieldErrors` renders a `<div>` listing the current field's validation errors. It is an ARIA live region, so errors that appear after page load are announced by screen readers, and its ID enters the input's `aria-describedby` (via the enclosing [Control](/docs/components/control)) only while errors exist.

For one error region per field, the [owned `fieldErrors` slot on Field](/docs/components/field) is usually simpler and SSR-safe. Use standalone `FieldErrors` when the errors must live elsewhere in the layout, or to set a per-container announcement policy with `live`.

## Live example

Submit empty to render the owned error region. Its ID joins `aria-describedby` while the error exists; a correct value removes the ID again while the container stays mounted.

<LiveFieldDemo />

## Minimal example

```svelte title="src/routes/settings/settings-form.svelte"
<script lang="ts">
	import { untrack } from "svelte";
	import { superForm, type SuperValidated } from "sveltekit-superforms";
	import { Control, Field, FieldErrors, Label } from "@emmorts/formsnap";
	import type { SettingsData } from "./schema.js";

	let { validated }: { validated: SuperValidated<SettingsData> } = $props();

	const form = superForm(untrack(() => validated));
	const { form: formData } = form;
</script>

<Field {form} name="email">
	<Control>
		{#snippet children({ props })}
			<Label>Email</Label>
			<input type="email" {...props} bind:value={$formData.email} />
		{/snippet}
	</Control>
	<FieldErrors />
</Field>
```

With no `children` or `child` snippet, each error renders as a `<div>` with `data-fs-field-error` and, while errors exist, `data-fs-error`.

## Custom error content

The `children` snippet receives the error list and an `errorProps` object to spread onto each error item, preserving the styling hooks:

```svelte title="src/routes/settings/styled-errors.svelte"
<Field {form} name="email">
	<Control>
		{#snippet children({ props })}
			<Label>Email</Label>
			<input type="email" {...props} bind:value={$formData.email} />
		{/snippet}
	</Control>
	<FieldErrors>
		{#snippet children({ errors, errorProps })}
			{#each errors as error, index (index)}
				<p {...errorProps} class="error">{error}</p>
			{/each}
		{/snippet}
	</FieldErrors>
</Field>
```

The `child` snippet goes further and replaces the outer container itself; it receives `props` (the container attributes), `errors` and `errorProps`. Spread `props` onto your container — those attributes register the mounted element and its ID with the field.

## Props

| Prop | Type | Default | Description |
| ---- | ---- | ------- | ----------- |
| `id` | `string` | generated | The container's ID. Generated with Svelte's `$props.id()` when omitted, stable between server rendering and hydration. |
| `ref` | `HTMLElement \| null` | `null` | Bindable reference to the rendered container. |
| `live` | `"assertive" \| "polite" \| "off"` | `"assertive"` | Announcement policy mirrored onto `aria-live`. Takes precedence over an `aria-live` attribute passed with the other props. |
| `children` | `Snippet<[{ errors, errorProps }]`> | — | Custom error content inside the default container. |
| `child` | `Snippet<[{ props, errors, errorProps }]`> | — | Replaces the container entirely; spread `props` onto your own element. |
| `...rest` | `HTMLAttributes<HTMLDivElement>` | — | Additional attributes merged onto the container. |

The merged container attributes are `id`, `aria-live`, `data-fs-field-errors`, and `data-fs-error` while errors exist.

## Behavior notes

- **Requires a field scope.** `FieldErrors` reads context from an enclosing [Field](/docs/components/field), [Fieldset](/docs/components/fieldset) or [ElementField](/docs/components/element-field); outside one it throws.
- **Live-region precedence.** Highest first: the `live` prop, then an `aria-live` attribute passed in `...rest`, then `"assertive"`. A spread `aria-live` is resolved before generated attributes merge, so it is never silently discarded — but `live` is the supported switch. `"off"` renders `aria-live="off"`, suppressing announcements while keeping the error association intact.
- **Association timing.** The container ID is included in the control's `aria-describedby` only while the field has errors. Like [Description](/docs/components/description), the standalone component registers on mount, so its association is not in server-rendered HTML — use the owned `fieldErrors` slot on the field scope for that.
- **Always mounted.** The container stays in the DOM while empty so the live region can announce errors as they appear.

## When to use the hooks instead

A custom control component can read `errors` and `errorsId` from `useFormField` and render its own error UI, declaring the container with the `errorsId` getter. Return `null` or `undefined` from the getter to withdraw the association. See [Error summary](/docs/recipes/error-summary) for collecting errors across fields, and [Custom controls](/docs/recipes/custom-controls) for the hook pattern.

## See also

- [Field](/docs/components/field) — its owned `fieldErrors` slot renders the same content with SSR-safe associations.
- [Description](/docs/components/description) — the non-error text also wired through `aria-describedby`.
- [Accessibility](/docs/guides/accessibility) — announcement policies and the association model.
